From feeda8c3b97da4d052d011f54f203ff13153b21f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleksii Zakharov <contact@zalexdev.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 08:10:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 22/60] um: correct three claims that were wrong in shipped
 text

Found by an audit of the series rather than by any failure. None changes
behaviour except the third; all three would have misled a reader.

The AT_MINSIGSTKSZ comment said the value is zero on "everything that is
not arm64". x86 has published it since v5.16 -- arch/x86/include/asm/elf.h
has three NEW_AUX_ENT sites, sized by get_sigframe_size(), which grows with
XSAVE state much as arm64's grows with the vector length. So the mechanism
is not arm64-specific and the comment said it was.

arch/arm64/um/Kconfig selected MODULES_USE_ELF_RELA. aarch64 modules are
RELA, but nothing here implements apply_relocate_add(), so the select
asserted a capability that does not exist and let allmodconfig and
randconfig get as far as failing to link. Drop it and say plainly that
modules are not supported yet.

The seccomp probe's new per-step diagnostic labelled its two most important
cases the wrong way round: exit 2 is sigaction() failing, which says
nothing about seccomp and everything about the probe, and was reported as
"missing"; exit 3 is SECCOMP_SET_MODE_FILTER refusing, which really does
mean this host has no seccomp, and was reported as "filter rejected". That
points the reader at the host when the bug is here -- exactly the failure
this diagnostic was added to prevent.

Also drop references to files outside the kernel tree from a header
comment, keeping the measurements they describe.

Signed-off-by: Oleksii Zakharov <contact@zalexdev.com>
---
 arch/arm64/um/Kconfig                     |  8 ++++-
 arch/arm64/um/shared/sysdep/ptrace_user.h | 10 +++---
 arch/um/os-Linux/elf_aux.c                | 24 +++++++++++++
 arch/um/os-Linux/start_up.c               | 44 +++++++++++++++++++++--
 4 files changed, 78 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

